---A Google Docs document.
---@class google_workspace.docs_v1.Document
---@field suggestedNamedStylesChanges? google_workspace.docs_v1.SuggestedNamedStylesMap Output only. The suggested changes to the named styles of the document, keyed by suggestion ID. Legacy field: Instead, use Document.tabs.documentTab.suggestedNamedStylesChanges, which exposes the actual document content from all tabs when the includeTabsContent parameter is set to `true`. If `false` or unset, this field contains information about the first tab in the document.
---@field revisionId? string Output only. The revision ID of the document. Can be used in update requests to specify which revision of a document to apply updates to and how the request should behave if the document has been edited since that revision. Only populated if the user has edit access to the document. The revision ID is not a sequential number but an opaque string. The format of the revision ID might change over time. A returned revision ID is only guaranteed to be valid for 24 hours after it has been returned and cannot be shared across users. If the revision ID is unchanged between calls, then the document has not changed. Conversely, a changed ID (for the same document and user) usually means the document has been updated. However, a changed ID can also be due to internal factors such as ID format changes.
---@field suggestedDocumentStyleChanges? google_workspace.docs_v1.SuggestedDocumentStyleMap Output only. The suggested changes to the style of the document, keyed by suggestion ID. Legacy field: Instead, use Document.tabs.documentTab.suggestedDocumentStyleChanges, which exposes the actual document content from all tabs when the includeTabsContent parameter is set to `true`. If `false` or unset, this field contains information about the first tab in the document.
---@field headers? google_workspace.docs_v1.HeaderMap Output only. The headers in the document, keyed by header ID. Legacy field: Instead, use Document.tabs.documentTab.headers, which exposes the actual document content from all tabs when the includeTabsContent parameter is set to `true`. If `false` or unset, this field contains information about the first tab in the document.
---@field suggestionsViewMode? google_workspace.docs_v1.DocumentSuggestionsViewModeEnum Output only. The suggestions view mode applied to the document. Note: When editing a document, changes must be based on a document with SUGGESTIONS_INLINE.
---@field namedStyles? google_workspace.docs_v1.NamedStyles Output only. The named styles of the document. Legacy field: Instead, use Document.tabs.documentTab.namedStyles, which exposes the actual document content from all tabs when the includeTabsContent parameter is set to `true`. If `false` or unset, this field contains information about the first tab in the document.
---@field body? google_workspace.docs_v1.Body Output only. The main body of the document. Legacy field: Instead, use Document.tabs.documentTab.body, which exposes the actual document content from all tabs when the includeTabsContent parameter is set to `true`. If `false` or unset, this field contains information about the first tab in the document.
---@field footnotes? google_workspace.docs_v1.FootnoteMap Output only. The footnotes in the document, keyed by footnote ID. Legacy field: Instead, use Document.tabs.documentTab.footnotes, which exposes the actual document content from all tabs when the includeTabsContent parameter is set to `true`. If `false` or unset, this field contains information about the first tab in the document.
---@field documentId? string Output only. The ID of the document.
---@field footers? google_workspace.docs_v1.FooterMap Output only. The footers in the document, keyed by footer ID. Legacy field: Instead, use Document.tabs.documentTab.footers, which exposes the actual document content from all tabs when the includeTabsContent parameter is set to `true`. If `false` or unset, this field contains information about the first tab in the document.
---@field comments? google_workspace.docs_v1.CommentThreadList Output only. The comments associated with the document. Only populated if the commentsViewMode parameter is set to require comments (such as `COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_INCLUDED`).
---@field namedRanges? google_workspace.docs_v1.NamedRangesMap Output only. The named ranges in the document, keyed by name. Legacy field: Instead, use Document.tabs.documentTab.namedRanges, which exposes the actual document content from all tabs when the includeTabsContent parameter is set to `true`. If `false` or unset, this field contains information about the first tab in the document.
---@field lists? google_workspace.docs_v1.ListMap Output only. The lists in the document, keyed by list ID. Legacy field: Instead, use Document.tabs.documentTab.lists, which exposes the actual document content from all tabs when the includeTabsContent parameter is set to `true`. If `false` or unset, this field contains information about the first tab in the document.
---@field suggestions? google_workspace.docs_v1.SuggestionThreadList Output only. The suggestions associated with the document. Only populated if the commentsViewMode parameter is set to require comments (such as `COMMENTS_VIEW_MODE_INCLUDED`).
---@field documentStyle? google_workspace.docs_v1.DocumentStyle Output only. The style of the document. Legacy field: Instead, use Document.tabs.documentTab.documentStyle, which exposes the actual document content from all tabs when the includeTabsContent parameter is set to `true`. If `false` or unset, this field contains information about the first tab in the document.
---@field positionedObjects? google_workspace.docs_v1.PositionedObjectMap Output only. The positioned objects in the document, keyed by object ID. Legacy field: Instead, use Document.tabs.documentTab.positionedObjects, which exposes the actual document content from all tabs when the includeTabsContent parameter is set to `true`. If `false` or unset, this field contains information about the first tab in the document.
---@field inlineObjects? google_workspace.docs_v1.InlineObjectMap Output only. The inline objects in the document, keyed by object ID. Legacy field: Instead, use Document.tabs.documentTab.inlineObjects, which exposes the actual document content from all tabs when the includeTabsContent parameter is set to `true`. If `false` or unset, this field contains information about the first tab in the document.
---@field commentsViewMode? google_workspace.docs_v1.DocumentCommentsViewModeEnum Output only. The comments view mode applied to the document.
---@field tabs? google_workspace.docs_v1.TabList Output only. Tabs that are part of a document. Tabs can contain child tabs, a tab nested within another tab. Child tabs are represented by the Tab.childTabs field.
---@field title? string The title of the document.

